WEBVTT

00:14.880 --> 00:18.000
Wow... What is this place?

00:18.670 --> 00:21.410
This is literally a mirror house...

00:22.930 --> 00:25.580
This is all made of ice,

00:25.580 --> 00:27.930
but it sure looks like a mirror.

00:27.930 --> 00:29.590
Come on.
Don't be confounded.

00:33.760 --> 00:34.590
Koki?

00:34.590 --> 00:37.140
Oh, it's nothing.

00:40.830 --> 00:42.000
Nothing...

00:49.700 --> 00:51.610
Hey, what's wrong, Koki?

00:53.330 --> 00:55.620
Did you hear something?

00:55.930 --> 00:58.620
Huh? Nah, nothing.

00:59.910 --> 01:01.000
That so...

01:17.770 --> 01:23.270
ARIFURETA - FROM COMMONPLACE
TO WORLD'S STRONGEST SEASON 3

02:35.010 --> 02:40.010
CHARGING EMOTIONS

02:54.500 --> 02:55.860
Wh-What?

02:56.150 --> 02:58.230
Did I scare you?

02:58.230 --> 02:59.830
My bad.

03:05.020 --> 03:06.270
Someone...

03:06.270 --> 03:07.660
Is someone here?

03:15.840 --> 03:16.630
Hey...

03:17.130 --> 03:18.570
Can't you hear it?

03:18.570 --> 03:20.530
It's like a person's voice...

03:20.530 --> 03:23.100
A whisper or something...

03:23.100 --> 03:26.730
Hey, Koki! Don't scare me like that!

03:27.510 --> 03:29.730
Does anyone hear something else?

03:30.210 --> 03:31.230
What about you, Shea?

03:31.610 --> 03:35.240
No, I'm not picking up anything.

03:35.630 --> 03:37.730
I can hear it clearly!

03:37.730 --> 03:40.650
Hey, aren't you just being too tense?

03:40.650 --> 03:42.590
Yeah... Maybe.

03:43.710 --> 03:48.420
Shea, let me know
if you feel or hear anything.

03:48.420 --> 03:49.250
Yes!

03:50.320 --> 03:51.460
There it is again...

03:51.460 --> 03:53.350
I'm not imagining it!

03:53.350 --> 03:54.760
I can hear it again!

03:55.220 --> 03:56.800
Koki?

03:56.800 --> 03:59.090
It's getting clearer now!

04:00.280 --> 04:02.330
The voice said,
"Are you sure you want this?"

04:02.690 --> 04:04.350
Well, Koki...

04:04.770 --> 04:06.730
I'm not hearing anything, though.

04:07.070 --> 04:10.480
M-Me neither.

04:10.830 --> 04:11.970
Right...

04:11.970 --> 04:14.000
I didn't hear anything either.

04:14.000 --> 04:16.630
I'm not lying! It's true!

04:16.630 --> 04:18.950
Damn, where are you?!
Enough hiding!

04:19.270 --> 04:22.390
How about you show yourself now?!

04:22.390 --> 04:23.180
Koki!

04:23.180 --> 04:25.130
Calm down, Koki!

04:25.130 --> 04:26.950
What's gotten into you?

04:27.370 --> 04:28.110
Shea.

04:28.110 --> 04:30.510
No, I couldn't pick up anything.

04:30.900 --> 04:33.480
Hajime, do you sense any magic reaction?

04:33.480 --> 04:35.210
No, nothing.

04:35.210 --> 04:40.360
Hmm... There might be a possibility that Koki
gave in to the pressure of the Labyrinth,

04:40.360 --> 04:43.210
slowly losing his sanity along the way...

04:43.210 --> 04:46.010
Still, isn't this too sudden?

04:58.460 --> 05:01.140
Amanogawa, calm down for now.

05:01.140 --> 05:03.580
Nagumo, I'm telling the truth!

05:03.580 --> 05:05.740
I... really...

05:06.400 --> 05:08.040
I know.

05:08.040 --> 05:10.750
I'm not trying to brush it off
as your imagination.

05:11.390 --> 05:12.290
Nagumo...

05:13.130 --> 05:15.580
Something is trying to
interfere with your mind.

05:15.580 --> 05:17.710
I suppose that's
the logical answer we must take.

05:17.710 --> 05:19.170
Huh?

05:19.780 --> 05:24.910
If the whispering voice is part
of the Labyrinth's trials,

05:24.910 --> 05:30.200
then it's highly possible that all of us will
be experiencing it, and not just Amanogawa.

05:31.440 --> 05:34.030
I don't know what the intention might be,

05:34.440 --> 05:37.560
but right now, we can't think of
anything to block it off.

05:37.940 --> 05:40.950
Anyway, be on your guard, guys.

05:44.940 --> 05:46.720
Didn't believe it, huh?

05:49.250 --> 05:50.450
Again...

05:51.300 --> 05:53.040
I remember this voice.

05:53.380 --> 05:55.190
Koki, are you okay?

05:55.190 --> 05:57.450
Yeah, I'm fine.

05:57.450 --> 05:59.260
I heard it again, but...

05:59.260 --> 06:00.050
But?

06:00.630 --> 06:02.310
It might just be me,

06:02.860 --> 06:05.410
but it sounds awfully familiar...

06:06.410 --> 06:08.310
Just like back in Haltina,

06:08.310 --> 06:11.320
it might be mimicking someone we know.

06:11.320 --> 06:13.770
Koki, don't get confused.

06:14.250 --> 06:17.320
I know.
You be careful as well, Shizuku.

06:17.880 --> 06:19.640
If what Nagumo said is true,

06:19.640 --> 06:22.070
maybe you'll eventually hear it too.

06:22.400 --> 06:24.310
I'll keep it in mind.

06:25.570 --> 06:27.290
You noticed, didn't you?

06:31.100 --> 06:33.290
Shizuku, did that...

06:33.290 --> 06:36.800
Yeah, I could hear it too.

06:37.570 --> 06:38.960
It was a girl's voice.

06:39.960 --> 06:42.340
It also sounds so familiar.

06:42.860 --> 06:45.680
She said,
"You looked the other way again, huh?"

06:48.070 --> 06:50.430
Where do you think
you're going back to?

06:51.530 --> 06:52.550
Oh...

06:53.330 --> 06:54.870
You could hear it too?

06:54.870 --> 06:57.670
I envy her so much,
I want to kill her...

07:01.350 --> 07:03.260
Oh, yeah.

07:03.260 --> 07:04.900
This is our own voice.

07:05.240 --> 07:06.580
Hajime?

07:06.580 --> 07:10.400
Amanogawa said he heard
a familiar voice whispering, right?

07:11.460 --> 07:13.030
You see,

07:13.030 --> 07:16.920
it sounds strange to hear your own voice,
so you may find it hard to notice.

07:17.480 --> 07:21.300
But that means,
what the voice is saying...

07:21.300 --> 07:24.470
Seems like everyone heard
the voice as well.

07:24.470 --> 07:27.990
Did you not notice it
from what it said?

07:27.990 --> 07:28.930
Huh?

07:30.920 --> 07:32.930
What did the voice say to you, Nagumo?

07:33.290 --> 07:34.030
Hmm?

07:34.420 --> 07:37.320
"There's no place for a monster like you."

07:37.320 --> 07:41.850
"Do you really think you can live
a normal life as a murderer?"

07:43.220 --> 07:46.250
Well, those words sure hurt me.

07:46.670 --> 07:48.830
It's hard to say that I'm still human.

07:50.610 --> 07:54.030
So, perhaps deep within,

07:54.030 --> 07:57.960
I think I'm no longer suited for
my previous life anymore.

07:59.130 --> 08:00.280
Nagumo...

08:04.190 --> 08:06.410
There's a small room up ahead.

08:06.410 --> 08:07.970
Let's get some rest there.

08:17.590 --> 08:20.520
Miss! I nominate Shizuku!

08:20.520 --> 08:21.440
Huh?

08:21.440 --> 08:22.270
SCHOOL ARTS FESTIVAL

08:22.270 --> 08:23.230
SCHOOL ARTS FESTIVAL
Hey.

08:23.590 --> 08:26.560
Shizuku, you'll be the princess.

08:26.560 --> 08:28.080
Come on.

08:28.080 --> 08:29.990
K-Kaori...

08:30.360 --> 08:33.990
You'll definitely look cute as the princess!

08:33.990 --> 08:37.500
Consider this our final good
memories of elementary school!

08:37.980 --> 08:39.170
But...

08:39.170 --> 08:43.620
If you're the princess,
then I want to be the knight.

08:43.620 --> 08:44.630
What do you think?

08:44.630 --> 08:46.130
In that case...

08:46.130 --> 08:48.140
Isn't it the other way around?

08:48.140 --> 08:48.600
Huh?

08:48.600 --> 08:52.170
Kaori should be the princess,
and Shizuku should be the knight!

08:52.170 --> 08:54.980
Shouldn't the knight be a guy?

08:54.980 --> 08:56.650
Yaegashi would look good as one!

08:56.650 --> 08:59.140
Right! She's good at kendo too!

08:59.140 --> 09:00.370
A girl knight!

09:00.370 --> 09:03.940
Um, I want Shizuku to be the princess...

09:03.940 --> 09:07.650
Now, now.
Let's not ignore Yaegashi.

09:08.030 --> 09:11.020
What do you want to play as, Yaegashi?

09:13.530 --> 09:14.950
I want to be the knight.

09:14.950 --> 09:16.910
Shizuku...

09:17.470 --> 09:19.910
Kaori's not cut out to be a knight.

09:20.640 --> 09:23.750
If she wields a sword, it'll be disaster.

09:23.750 --> 09:25.590
SCHOOL ARTS FESTIVAL

09:29.880 --> 09:31.850
You prioritise someone else...

09:31.850 --> 09:33.410
...giving up your own emotions...

09:33.900 --> 09:35.310
Does that make you happy?

09:36.200 --> 09:38.630
Yaegashi, I'll leave the rest to you.

09:38.630 --> 09:40.940
Sure, you got it.

09:41.820 --> 09:43.860
You can handle this much, right, Yaegashi?

09:43.860 --> 09:45.020
Of course.

09:45.400 --> 09:48.020
You really can do anything, Shizuku.

09:50.250 --> 09:52.550
You're not going anywhere, right, Shizuku?

09:52.550 --> 09:53.930
No.

09:58.740 --> 10:00.500
Just like that...

10:00.500 --> 10:04.290
You will always be relied on,
bound to them...

10:04.860 --> 10:06.350
And protect them...

10:06.350 --> 10:07.060
Stop!

10:07.060 --> 10:09.230
You will be alone.

10:09.230 --> 10:11.060
That's not true!

10:17.360 --> 10:19.220
Who... are you?

10:19.890 --> 10:23.980
See? You are not in that sunlight.

10:35.110 --> 10:36.590
Oh, right...

10:36.590 --> 10:39.070
We were taking a short break...

10:39.070 --> 10:41.500
Shizushizu, what's up?

10:41.500 --> 10:44.640
Huh? Oh, it's nothing.

10:44.640 --> 10:47.380
Anyway, how about you?
Are you okay?

10:47.380 --> 10:50.010
Shizushizu, don't force yourself.

10:50.010 --> 10:52.380
I'll listen to your problems, if you want.

10:52.380 --> 10:55.230
What a worrywart you are, Suzu.

10:55.610 --> 10:57.820
If anything, you're looking in pain.

10:58.350 --> 10:59.840
Are you really okay?

11:00.880 --> 11:02.980
I'm okay...

11:02.980 --> 11:04.500
Shizuku.

11:04.500 --> 11:06.690
You must be selfish sometimes.

11:06.690 --> 11:07.430
Huh?

11:07.860 --> 11:09.690
What's that supposed to mean?

11:09.690 --> 11:14.190
I'll be happy to listen
to any of your whims.

11:17.890 --> 11:19.170
Hey, Koki.

11:19.170 --> 11:20.030
What?

11:20.370 --> 11:23.000
Oh, it's nothing, actually.

11:23.550 --> 11:27.500
I'm just raring to leave
this creepy place already.

11:28.700 --> 11:30.000
Right...

11:43.030 --> 11:45.850
Still seeking for help even here?

11:46.450 --> 11:48.230
That's why he'll take it away from you.

11:51.400 --> 11:53.820
Koki! Calm down for a sec!

11:54.240 --> 11:56.230
I am calm!

12:06.880 --> 12:07.920
Koki?!

12:09.630 --> 12:11.340
An enemy!

12:11.760 --> 12:15.440
My reflection on the wall just smirked!

12:15.440 --> 12:17.160
Even though I didn't...

12:17.630 --> 12:19.970
It's like somebody else was inside!

12:21.850 --> 12:23.510
You sure you weren't seeing things?

12:23.510 --> 12:25.150
You don't believe me?!

12:25.150 --> 12:28.520
No, I'm not doubting you.

12:28.910 --> 12:30.280
When it comes to Nagumo...

12:30.920 --> 12:33.820
When it comes to him,
you'd just believe him straight, huh?

12:34.450 --> 12:36.660
What are you really on about?

12:36.660 --> 12:38.950
I told you, I'm not doubting you.

12:40.290 --> 12:42.400
Sorry, Shizuku...

12:51.870 --> 12:53.610
Looks like we've arrived.

13:02.130 --> 13:03.980
That's our next door.

13:04.810 --> 13:06.760
It already looks suspicious from here.

13:06.760 --> 13:09.570
I have a really bad feeling about this.

13:09.570 --> 13:11.010
Yes.

13:11.010 --> 13:15.860
It's already an established theory
to be ambushed in a huge space.

13:15.860 --> 13:19.930
Rather, they must plan to use
this huge space exactly to attack.

13:19.930 --> 13:22.320
Well, only one way forward.

13:32.640 --> 13:33.500
Tch...

13:48.370 --> 13:49.850
Kick about!

13:51.900 --> 13:53.890
Looks like it's not just mere ice.

13:53.890 --> 13:54.730
Yeah.

13:54.730 --> 13:56.980
If one strike isn't enough,

13:56.980 --> 13:58.990
then how about consecutive strikes!

13:59.570 --> 14:02.930
My breath shall fend off
the attacks like ice!

14:04.250 --> 14:05.280
Sonic Slice!

14:05.650 --> 14:06.950
Dismantle!

14:06.950 --> 14:08.950
Rrraaagh!

14:08.950 --> 14:10.910
Here I go!

14:11.270 --> 14:13.040
Celestial Flash!

14:18.650 --> 14:19.840
Noo!

14:23.380 --> 14:24.640
Tch...

14:25.760 --> 14:27.490
What was that for?

14:27.490 --> 14:29.850
Kaori, you've got some guts.

14:29.850 --> 14:33.980
M-Miss Shizuku?! Have I annoyed you?!

14:33.980 --> 14:35.520
N-No!

14:35.520 --> 14:38.040
I didn't mean to attack you at all!

14:38.490 --> 14:39.770
When I came to...

14:40.270 --> 14:41.420
I'm telling the truth!

14:41.420 --> 14:43.560
Yeah, he's right!

14:43.560 --> 14:46.330
We'd never try to attack you!

14:46.330 --> 14:47.490
That's a matter of course!

14:47.920 --> 14:51.990
Sorry, Shea, but I don't even know myself.

14:51.990 --> 14:53.980
I was about to slash my enemy...

14:54.810 --> 14:57.730
Hajime, looks like we've been led on.

14:57.730 --> 15:01.880
I think I heard a whisper
right before attacking.

15:03.230 --> 15:05.340
This is trouble, Master.

15:05.900 --> 15:06.730
Perhaps...

15:07.160 --> 15:09.350
...they are interfering with
our subconsciousness.

15:09.700 --> 15:13.350
The whispering voices are a kind of imprinting.

15:13.970 --> 15:17.190
So that explains their attacks dispersing.

15:17.780 --> 15:19.650
In that case, how do we remove it...

15:20.370 --> 15:22.850
It is surely not magical effects alone.

15:22.850 --> 15:24.400
This is difficult.

15:26.050 --> 15:27.490
What a pain.

15:28.490 --> 15:29.580
Huh?

15:29.970 --> 15:31.910
I'll just blow it all to pieces.

15:55.270 --> 15:57.060
Hey...

16:01.860 --> 16:05.320
Oh, Mister Hajime,
we're losing one over there.

16:05.320 --> 16:06.790
Oh, I get it now...

16:06.790 --> 16:09.450
Looks like each of us
has to take down one,

16:09.450 --> 16:11.650
or they'll just endlessly come back.

16:12.230 --> 16:14.410
Then, I'll deal with them now!

16:14.810 --> 16:16.410
Celestial Flash!

16:30.690 --> 16:32.380
What do we have to do now?!

16:32.380 --> 16:33.760
Don't waver!

16:34.170 --> 16:35.890
Don't think, just get them!

16:40.560 --> 16:44.270
So I've cleared the trial, huh...

16:44.270 --> 16:48.750
Shizuku, Suzu, Ryutaro, Koki!

16:48.750 --> 16:51.640
We're okay!
Focus on your own enemy!

16:51.640 --> 16:52.280
Okay!

16:54.410 --> 16:57.120
So you're my enemy?

16:58.360 --> 17:00.730
I can hear the whispering...

17:06.090 --> 17:07.010
Huh?!

17:09.090 --> 17:11.490
Kaori, no need to hold back!

17:11.490 --> 17:13.640
I won't either!

17:13.640 --> 17:15.660
Sorry about this!

17:19.310 --> 17:22.940
A dismantle barrage should be able
to settle the score with one strike,

17:22.940 --> 17:25.290
but if I'm led on again...

17:27.000 --> 17:30.570
Is Yue done? That means I won't have
to worry about disturbing her...

17:34.030 --> 17:37.440
Yue! Deflect it at 45 degrees!

17:48.300 --> 17:49.460
Nice...

18:04.050 --> 18:06.070
Tear them, Sonic Flash!

18:08.010 --> 18:08.970
Shea!

18:08.970 --> 18:11.450
Oh, don't worry about me!

18:11.450 --> 18:14.160
I really can't use long-range skills...

18:14.980 --> 18:15.820
In that case...

18:16.370 --> 18:18.260
Cut them off, Flash Blitz!

18:19.380 --> 18:21.270
Destroy them, Shock Slugger!

18:22.600 --> 18:24.650
Crush them, Gravity Flash!

18:36.010 --> 18:37.420
It's over.

18:37.940 --> 18:38.970
Shock Slugger!

18:47.070 --> 18:48.420
I'm still terrible...

18:48.820 --> 18:49.810
...on my own.

18:49.810 --> 18:51.280
Shizuku...

18:58.950 --> 19:02.130
What? Got something to say?

19:02.130 --> 19:03.910
Nah.

19:03.910 --> 19:07.460
I just thought you guys are so close.

19:07.460 --> 19:10.790
Right. What a lovely friendship.

19:10.790 --> 19:14.720
Yes. It really soothes the heart.

19:14.720 --> 19:17.470
You're just like lovers.

19:17.470 --> 19:20.970
Yue, don't mock me like that again.

19:20.970 --> 19:23.270
Fear not, Kaori.

19:23.270 --> 19:25.380
I have no prejudices.

19:25.970 --> 19:28.800
Love between girls is a valid thing, I think.

19:29.180 --> 19:30.980
I hope you two will be happy forever.

19:33.940 --> 19:35.150
Nagumo!

19:35.150 --> 19:36.240
I'll be fine.

19:40.370 --> 19:43.560
Amanogawa sure is rushing it.

19:43.560 --> 19:44.830
How are they doing?

19:45.430 --> 19:48.320
They still have techniques
from Limit Break, right?

19:48.320 --> 19:51.670
If they haven't used those,
that means it should be easy.

19:52.360 --> 19:54.780
Take a few minutes,
and they'll clear it.

19:55.340 --> 19:57.370
That includes Sakagami and Taniguchi.

20:07.130 --> 20:08.570
Look after them, Kaori.

20:08.570 --> 20:10.340
Got it.

20:16.300 --> 20:19.590
Looks like this is the way out.

20:20.510 --> 20:22.390
It looks like a gate...

20:22.390 --> 20:24.600
A teleport exit?

20:24.600 --> 20:27.290
I'm not feeling good about this.

20:27.290 --> 20:28.350
Shea.

20:28.350 --> 20:28.960
Huh?

20:28.960 --> 20:32.550
We have never had a good feeling
when it comes to a Great Labyrinth, right?

20:34.080 --> 20:35.260
You have a point...

20:35.870 --> 20:38.260
Should we rest up for a bit here,

20:38.260 --> 20:39.850
or we push forward?

20:39.850 --> 20:41.020
Which one will it be?

20:41.020 --> 20:42.260
Let's push forward.

20:44.630 --> 20:46.980
That so? Let's go, then.

21:00.320 --> 21:02.150
So it's divided into parts, huh?

21:02.150 --> 21:04.660
Well, I kinda had
a feeling that'd be that case.

21:35.800 --> 21:37.120
Oh, no...

21:37.120 --> 21:39.470
Now that I actually notice it,
I feel terrible...

21:40.040 --> 21:42.450
What a chuni I am...

21:43.070 --> 21:45.380
I guess it's just like the voice said.

21:45.380 --> 21:48.330
Maybe I don't have a place in Japan.

21:49.450 --> 21:51.950
That's not what I mean.

21:54.090 --> 21:55.710
You finally came out...

23:32.970 --> 23:34.830
TRUE HEART

23:34.830 --> 23:37.650
TRUE HEART
Next episode: True Heart.

23:37.650 --> 23:40.940
TRUE HEART
